<title>USA: GM September US domestic car sales fall.</title>
<headline>GM September US domestic car sales fall.</headline>
<dateline>DETROIT 1996-10-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>General Motors Corp Thursday reported the following U.S. sales data for month of September:</p>
<p>			Sep 1-30, 1996     Sep 1-30, 1995 *Pct Chng</p>
<p> Domestic Car	   223,867	   262,553	    -11.2</p>
<p> Domestic Truck	 149,482	   137,089	    +13.6</p>
<p> Import Car		 2,873	     2,282	    +31.1</p>
<p> Import Truck		 206		 218	     -1.6</p>
<p>		  Jan 1-Sep 30, 1996 Jan 1-Sep 30, 1995 *Pct Chng</p>
<p> Domestic Car	 2,201,368	 2,234,860	     -1.9</p>
<p> Domestic Truck     1,487,990	 1,430,561	     +3.6</p>
<p> Import Car		22,574	    20,433	    +10.0</p>
<p> Import Truck	     2,249	     2,668	    -16.1</p>
<p>* Pct change based on daily selling rate. Sale days 24 in latest month vs 25, 231 for year to date vs 230 in year ago.  </p>
<p>NOTE: Import car figures are all sales from Saab Automobile AB, which is 50 percent owned by GM, except for 51 cars in the 1995 year-to-date total.</p>
</text>
